WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
Colloquial Tamil by R.E. Asher and E. Annamalai.

00:04.500 --> 00:07.500
Copyright R.E. Asher and E. Annamalai.

00:07.500 --> 00:12.500
Recording copyright Routledge Limited 2002.

00:12.500 --> 00:15.500
Welcome to Colloquial Tamil.

00:15.500 --> 00:22.500
This recording begins with a section on pronunciation based on the section on pronunciation in the introduction to the accompanying book.

00:22.500 --> 00:30.500
This part focuses on those Tamil sounds to which the beginner needs to pay particular attention, generally because they are unfamiliar to most speakers of English.

00:30.500 --> 00:37.000
These pronunciation points are reinforced from time to time in later parts of the recording.

00:37.000 --> 00:41.500
The recording continues with all the dialogues and other texts in the book.

00:41.500 --> 00:48.500
There are also exercises from the book, along with some additional exercises for practice in listening comprehension and in speaking.

00:48.500 --> 00:56.000
Where the tape contains material which is taken unchanged from the book, you may well listen to it with the book open in front of you.

00:56.000 --> 01:03.500
However, you should also make a habit of listening without the help of the written text in order to increase your understanding of the spoken form.

01:03.500 --> 01:10.000
When you are specifically asked to repeat a word or phrase, there is a short pause on the tape.

01:10.000 --> 01:21.000
But you should use the pause button to repeat other phrases and longer utterances in order to give yourself lots of practice in speaking and understanding.